According to the documented rule for conformance.kernel.recovery, 'The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text' [4adba2f4da302fee]. In the input, the second code fence holds object B, so it is the scored object. In the rewritten text, the second code fence is empty, so the rule falls back to the last object inside a code fence that holds one, which is object A in the first fence. Thus the recovered object moves from {"b": 2} to {"a": 1}.